परि-√ 5. वस् P. -वसति, (ind.p. पर्य्-उष्य), to abide, stay, remain with (instr.), KātyŚr.; R. &c.;
 (with संसर्गितया) to associate with (acc.), Kull. on Mn. xi, 190 :
Caus. वासयति, to let stand overnight, ĀśvGṛ.

परि-√ वह् P. -वहति (Pāṇ. i, 3, 82, Sch.), to carry about or round, RV. &c. &c.;
to drag about, MBh.;
to flow around, TS.; Āpast.;
to lead home the nuptial train or the bride, take to wife, marry (Pass. -उह्य॑ते, p. -उह्य॑मान), RV.; BhP.

परि-√ 3. विद् P. -विन्दति, to find out, ascertain, Hariv.;
to twine, twist round (see below);
to marry before an elder brother (only Pass. यया [Mn. iii, 172] or या [MBh. xii, 6108] परि-विद्यते, [the woman] with whom such a marriage is contracted).

परि-√ विष् P. -वेषति, MBh. (mostly Intens. -वेवेष्टि Subj. -वेविषति Pot. -वेविष्यात्, AV.; Br.; Kāṭh.; -वेविषाणि, -{{अवेविषत्->अवेविषम्ळ्ह्ळ्ह्२०२६०६२३ळ्ह्श्चोत्त् ण्होदेस्ळ्ह्ह्त्त्प्स्:॑꣡गित्हुब्।चोम्॑सन्स्क्रित्-लेऌइचोन्॑च्स्ल्-चोर्रेच्तिओन्स्॑इस्सुएस्॑२७३}}}, Pāṇ. vii, 3, 87, Sch.; Ā. fut. p. -वेक्ष्यमाण, KātyŚr.; BhP.; ind.p. -वि॑ष्य, AV.; Ved. inf. -वि॑षे, RV.),
to serve, wait on, offer or dress food:
Pass. -विष्यते, to be served &c., MBh.;
 to have a halo (said of sun or moon), ṢaḍvBr.; Gobh.; Hariv. :
Caus. -वेषयति (ind.p. -वेष्य, also written -वेश्˚), to offer food, wait on (acc.), Mn. iii, 228; MBh.; R.; BhP.;
to dress food, Campak.

परि-√ वृज् P. -वृणक्ति (Impv. -वृङ्धि, -वृणक्तु; aor. Subj. -वर्जति Pot. -वृज्यात्),
to turn out of the way of (acc.), avoid, shun, spare, pass over, RV.; AV.; VS.; Br.; Āpast.;
to cast out, expel, AitBr.;
 (Ā.) to surround, enclose, BhP. :
Caus. -वर्जयति, ˚ते (ind.p. -वर्ज्य), to keep off, remove, AV.;
to avoid, shun, quit, abandon, not heed, disregard, Mn.; MBh. &c.

परि-√ वृत् Ā. -वर्तते (ep. also ˚ति; ind.p. -वृत्य, or परी-वर्तम्),
to turn round, revolve, move in a circle or to and fro, roll or wheel or wander about, circumambulate (acc.), RV. &c. &c.;
 (with हृदि or हृदये) to run in a person's mind, MBh.;
to return, go or come back to (acc.), ib.;
to be reborn in (loc.), VP.;
 (also with अन्यथा) to change, turn out different, MBh.; Kāv.;
to abide, stay, remain, Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to act, proceed, behave, R. :
Caus. -वर्तयति, to cause to turn or move round or back or to and fro, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
 (Ā.) to roll or bring near (Subj. -वर्तयाते), RV. v, 37, 3;
to overthrow, upset (a carriage), Hariv.;
to invert, put in a reverse order, Mṛcch. v, 9/10 (read -वर्त्य for -वृत्य);
to change, barter, exchange, MBh.; Hariv. &c.;
to renew (an agreement), Mn. viii, 154 &c.;
to understand or explain wrongly (words &c.), MBh.; Kāv.;
to turn topsy-turvy i.e. search thoroughly, R.;
to destroy, annihilate, ib.;
to straiten, contract, Car.;
 (Ā.) to cause one's self to be turned round (in having one's head shaved all round), TBr.; ŚBr. (cf. -वर्तन) :
Intens. -व॑वर्त्ति, to turn (intrans.) continually, RV. i, 164, 11.

परि-√ वृध् Ā. -वर्धते, to grow, grow up, increase, Kāv.; Rājat.; Suśr. :
Caus. -वर्धयति, ˚ते, to bring up, rear, increase, augment, MBh.; Kāv.;
to rejoice, delight (with gen.), Hariv.

परि-√ व्ये P. Ā. -व्ययति, ˚ते (aor. -अव्यत, -व्यत, RV.; ind.p. -व्याय and -वीय cf. Pāṇ. vi, 1, 44),
to wrap or tie round;
 (Ā.) to wrap one's self up, RV.; &c.

परि-√ व्रज् P. -व्रजति (ind.p. -व्रज्य), to go or wander about, walk round, circumambulate (acc.), ŚBr.; GṛŚrS. &c.;
to wander about as a religious mendicant, Up.; Mn.; MBh. &c.;
 (with Jainas) to become a recluse, HPariś. :
Caus. -व्राजयति, to cause a person to become a recluse, ib.
